{"id":"taiwan-round-island","title":"Round Taiwan by bike (Huandao)","who":"Classic route · Taiwan's national cycling rite","when":"October to April (ride anticlockwise in winter)","vehicle":"Road or touring bike, 9–14 days","kind":"bike","color":"#dc2626","summary":"About 950 km around the island, a rite of passage in Taiwan: the busy west coast and its night markets, the tropical south at Kenting, the Shouka pass, the rice paddies of the East Rift Valley on Highway 9, and the marble cliffs of the Pacific coast. 7-Elevens every few kilometres and bike-friendly police stations. The Suhua Highway (Highway 9) north of Hualien had rockslide and mudslide closures in 2026; many riders take the train for that stretch.","sources":[{"label":"Focus Taiwan: rockslide damages a Suhua Highway tunnel (April 2026)","url":"https://focustaiwan.tw/society/202604260006"},{"label":"Albinger: a bike ride around Taiwan, part 2, the east coast (2025 trip)","url":"https://albinger.me/2026/01/10/a-bike-ride-around-taiwan-part-2-the-east-coast/"},{"label":"CycleBlaze: Yuli south to Taitung City (January 2025)","url":"https://cycleblaze.com/journals/2025cny/yuli-south-to-taitung-city"}],"approximate":"Main towns, anticlockwise; the line follows Route 1 and 9 roughly.","km":1035,"bbox":[120.1255,21.9452,121.958,25.1091],"stops":[{"name":"Taipei","place":"Taipei, Taiwan","at":[25.0375,121.5637],"text":"The start under Taipei 101."},{"name":"Hsinchu","place":"Hsinchu, Taiwan","at":[24.8066,120.9687],"text":"The windy city of the west coast.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/%E6%96%B0%E7%AB%B9%E7%81%AB%E8%BB%8A%E7%AB%99%28%E5%B7%B4%E6%B4%9B%E5%85%8B%E9%A2%A8%E6%A0%BC%29.jpg/500px-%E6%96%B0%E7%AB%B9%E7%81%AB%E8%BB%8A%E7%AB%99%28%E5%B7%B4%E6%B4%9B%E5%85%8B%E9%A2%A8%E6%A0%BC%29.jpg","page":"Hsinchu","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%96%B0%E7%AB%B9%E7%81%AB%E8%BB%8A%E7%AB%99%28%E5%B7%B4%E6%B4%9B%E5%85%8B%E9%A2%A8%E6%A0%BC%29.jpg","credit":